{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-348849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{8x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{3}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{3}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{3}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-348849" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348849" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{5}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{5}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I \\\\ 6I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{6}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{6}-{0}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{243}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-348618" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-348618" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{243}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{9}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{9}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I \\\\ 10I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡(e)-{ln}^{10}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{40}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{40}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{6}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{6}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I \\\\ 7I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡(e)-{ln}^{7}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7"] ["math" "7e"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{12}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-114952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-49609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2I) \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{3}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{6x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6{e}^{6x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(6{e}^{6x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{6x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6{e}^{6x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(6{e}^{6x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6({e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6I) \\\\ I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-36I \\\\ 37I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{37}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1bb557360bbee7325bccf0113aaf885633ba56b2616e357717414460c45b3b7b"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "37\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{7}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{37}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{6x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-15421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{37}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-12919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-12919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{13}{9}I & =\\frac{3{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042486/state.json" "file_sha256" "148f879e50920bbb60c00776e8408455ebe5df66683637a8801cf3ae2f787049"} {"question" "q-12919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "v